{"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivortuning\/tuningsystem\/kirnbergerii"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/TuningSystem"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"kirnbergerII","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WellTemperament","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament"},{"text":" { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Two fifths — D→A and A→E — are each narrowed by ½ of the syntonic comma, equal to","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"√(20\/9) ≈ 691.202 cents. One fifth — F♯→C♯ — is narrowed by one schisma"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(32805:32768), equal to 16384:10935 ≈ 699.977 cents. The remaining nine fifths are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pure (3:2). The circle closes exactly because one syntonic comma times one schisma"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"equals one Pythagorean comma."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The two half-comma fifths are unusually flat, giving C-adjacent keys very pure"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"thirds while keys with many sharps or flats suffer greatly."}]}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/TuningSystem\/kirnbergerII","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"metadata":{"